 "_note": "11-08 TEMPORAL-CONTACT variant of R3B (rr_T1k_r3B_s5.json; everything else identical). No demo contact labels in the reward: contact_set / contact_graph (T1/T2 vs the reference) 0 and free_finger_acc 0 (its free-finger mask comes from the reference contact labels; finger_still, which uses the reference finger speed, stays 1.0). New, from the policy's own contacts between consecutive control steps: contact_keep 0.5 (fraction of the previous step's contacts lost; hysteresis: in at > 0.1 x weight, out at < 0.05 x weight), contact_drift 0.5 (mean change of the pairwise contact distances on the object, 1 = 1 mm per step, plunger stroke undone), contact_slip 0.5 (mean motion of each contact point on the object, 1 = 1 mm per step). The three are off during the deliberate in-hand regrasps (temporal_off_gates: gate_grasp_shift_right / _left, gate_regrasp of reference.npz). wrench_support (T3, blind to torque balance) 0, replaced by wrench_margin 0.5 (required wrench of the reference object motion +- 0.3 N on each wrench axis must lie in what the contacts can supply with <= 3 N per contact, circular cones mu 1.5; solved every 4 control steps; only while the reference holds the object). Requires the task meshes (scene does not compile in this checkout). wall_hours 10.0 (R3B: 3.0) only as a cap: the run is meant to end at max_env_steps 2e8 like R3B (1.97e8 in 2.85 h on the authors' GPU; slower on a 4080).",
